**Plan: parse the flag in `cli.js`, add `toJson` to `format.js`, leave `report.js` alone.**

One call to make. The table drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose, for width. JSON has no width limit. I'd print the full `buildRows()` row, six fields, not the four columns.

```js
// cli.js
const json = argv.includes('--json');
const rows = buildRows();
process.stdout.write((json ? toJson(rows) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');

// format.js
function toJson(rows) { return JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2); }
```

Say the word if you want JSON limited to the four table columns instead.
